WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
RYAN MATSUMOTO: Hi.

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.060
My name is Ryan, and
I'd like to show you

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.120
how to get started with
Google Cloud at no charge.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.800
In the next few
minutes, we'll talk

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.050
about how you can get
started with the free trial,

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.560
the free tier, and Google
Maps Platform monthly credits.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.430
Ready?

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.270
Let's get started.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.532
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.510
As you start exploring
Google Cloud,

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:27.040
you may want to take advantage
of our 90-day, $300 free trial.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.650
The free trial provides you
with free Cloud billing credits

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.310
to pay for resources used while
you learn about Google Cloud.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.350
You can activate the free
trial if you've never

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.810
been a paying customer of
Google Cloud, Google Maps

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.750
Platform, or Firebase, and
if you haven't previously

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.960
signed up for the free trial.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.260
To start, visit
console.cloud.google.com

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.930
to open the Google
Cloud Console.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.390
This is where you can manage
your Google Cloud resources

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.850
directly from the web.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.890
Log in with the Google
account of your choice

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.710
and accept the terms
and conditions.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.480
At the top of your
screen, you see

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.460
a banner about the free trial.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.070
Click Activate to continue.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.050
Select your country,
tell us what

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.540
best describes your
organization or needs,

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.610
and accept the terms of service.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.130
Then click Continue.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.120
After verifying
your phone number,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.640
choose between a
Business account

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.950
or an Individual account.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.290
Then you're asked to provide
credit card information.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.340
But don't worry.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.680
You won't be charged
unless you manually upgrade

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.230
to a paid account later on.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.330
Click Start my free
trial to activate it.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.340
Now you have $300 in free
credits for the first 90 days

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.800
to use across all
of Google Cloud.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.930
You can do things like
create new Compute Engine

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:51.020
virtual machines, deploy
serverless applications

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:56.420
to Cloud Run, and set up new
Cloud SQL database instances.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.040
Throughout the
free trial period,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.757
your available credits
and days remaining

00:01:59.757 --> 00:02:02.090
are displayed in the billing
section of the Google Cloud

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.710
Console.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.930
And, if you upgrade to
a paid account later on,

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.030
you'll be able to keep
your Cloud resources

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.510
and use any remaining credits.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.400
Beyond the free
trial, there's also

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.010
the free tier, which lets
you use certain Google Cloud

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.300
products free of charge within
specified monthly usage limits.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.540
The free tier is available to
both new and existing users

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.750
and includes products
like App Engine, BigQuery,

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.040
Cloud Functions, Cloud
Vision, Firestore, and more.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.800
With BigQuery, for example,
you get 10 gigabytes

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.730
of storage per month and 1
terabyte of querying per month.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.040
If you're using the
free trial, any usage

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.870
of products within
the free tier will not

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.060
be deducted from your
$300 free trial credits.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.420
And, if you've already
upgraded to a paid account,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.220
any usage of products
within the free tier

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.980
will not be charged
to your credit card.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.500
Finally, the Google
Cloud free program

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.800
includes $200 of monthly
credits to use with Google Maps

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.550
Platform products.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.280
This allows you
to explore and use

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.540
powerful APIs for maps,
routes, and places.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.910
So there you have it, an
overview of how you can get

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.860
started with Google
Cloud at no charge

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.340
using the free trial, the free
tier, and Google Maps Platform

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.600
credits.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.210
Make sure to check out the
other episodes of "Google Cloud

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.430
Essentials," where we
cover the Google Cloud

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:24.450
Console, the Google Cloud
SDK, key use cases, and more.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.900
I can't wait to see what
you build with Google Cloud.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

